  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written to `/app` and validated. Everything reconciles \u2014 the per-finding counts sum to `finding_total` (23), flagged+compliant = request_count (28), and the account rollup totals match the batch figures.\n\n**Audit summary (INT-09, as of 2026-03-31):**\n\n- `composite_request_audit.csv` \u2014 28 audited requests (4 withdrawn rows excluded); 14 clean (`none`), 14 flagged; findings `;`-joined in policy rule order.\n- `account_summary.csv` \u2014 8 accounts, one row each; total 28 requests, 14 flagged.\n- `composite_request_memo.md` \u2014 standalone memo covering the audit date, out-of-scope (withdrawn) requests, every flagged request with its deciding record, requests the numbers would flag but the policy clears, master-agreement standing, and the \u00a78 decisions.\n- `results.json` \u2014 the eleven \u00a79 figures, each a single number.\n\n**Headline figures:** request_count 28 \u00b7 account_count 8 \u00b7 flagged 14 \u00b7 compliant 14 \u00b7 finding_total 23 \u00b7 character 6 \u00b7 background 5 \u00b7 consent 3 \u00b7 commercial 6 \u00b7 disclosure 3 \u00b7 escalated_accounts 4.\n\n**Key calls for Thursday:**\n- Two renewals *narrowed* rights \u2014 LIC-109 cut the Rook and Raven cap 35%\u219220% (cost REQ-05) and LIC-110 cut Old Quarry scope `all`\u2192`print_for_sale` (cost REQ-28).\n- Lapsed agreements clear nothing \u2014 ACC-04 and ACC-08 route despite naming channels; ACC-08 names the exact channel REQ-30 uses.\n- The personal-use allowance is \u00a73-only \u2014 REQ-32's 55% character area is released, but its missing minor consent still raises a finding.\n- \u00a78 escalations: ACC-02 and ACC-03 (each holds a 3-finding request), ACC-07 and ACC-08 (flagged share 66.7% > 50% batch share); ACC-01/04/05 sit exactly on 50% and do not escalate.\n\nAll four files confirmed present in `/app`.",
